<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#old-kannada">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Old Kannada</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Halegannada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a>, or Halegannada, is the form of the Kannada language used in inscriptions and literature of the later first and early second millennium CE, from the Rashtrakuta period to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a>. Its classical works include the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kavirajamarga">Kavirajamarga</a> of the 9th century and the poems of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adikavi-pampa">Pampa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranna">Ranna</a>, and Kesiraja's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shabdamanidarpana">Shabdamanidarpana</a> of about 1260 is its standard grammar.</p></div>
